# Inputs for constraints.txt: the Python packages that the deployable runtime and CI install.
#
# Scope: CPython 3.12 on Linux. It covers every `pip install -c constraints.txt` consumer: the
# API and Worker images, the CI jobs and `make install`, plus Playwright for the browser runtime
# job. Provider SDK extras (openai, anthropic, ...) are not included because no consumer installs
# them, and uv.lock is a different scope (the whole workspace with every extra).
#
# Regenerate with `make lock-constraints` and check with `make lock-constraints-check`.
-r apps/api/requirements.txt
-r apps/api/requirements-dev.txt
-r apps/worker-orchestrator/requirements.txt
-r apps/worker-orchestrator/requirements-dev.txt
./packages/creator-domain
./packages/creator-provider
./packages/creator-service
playwright
